1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,850
How do you build

2
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:03,110
a 726-foot dam

3
00:00:03,110 --> 00:00:04,550
inside a flowing river?

4
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:06,410
In the 1930s,

5
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:08,110
engineers faced this challenge

6
00:00:08,110 --> 00:00:09,110
at Black Canyon.

7
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:10,970
Before building anything,

8
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,180
they had to move

9
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:13,410
the Colorado River.

10
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:16,190
Crews blasted four huge tunnels

11
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:17,500
through the canyon walls.

12
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:19,650
Combined, those tunnels stretched

13
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:21,110
almost three miles

14
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:22,040
around the worksite.

15
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:24,540
Next, temporary cofferdams

16
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:25,460
blocked the river

17
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,110
and kept the foundation dry.

18
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:29,320
Excavators dug through sediment

19
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,280
until they reached solid bedrock.

20
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:33,220
Above them, high scalers

21
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:34,170
hung from ropes,

22
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:36,450
clearing unstable canyon walls.

23
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:38,270
In 1933,

24
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:40,030
crews began pouring concrete,

25
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,070
not as one giant slab,

26
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:43,100
but in hundreds

27
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,720
of interlocking blocks,

28
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,260
rising layer by layer.

29
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,760
Engineers circulated chilled water

30
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:49,940
through embedded pipes

31
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:51,090
to prevent overheating.

32
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:52,870
The dam alone required

33
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:55,700
3.25 million cubic yards

34
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:56,380
of concrete.

35
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:57,930
The concrete was finished

36
00:00:57,930 --> 00:00:59,370
in 1935;

37
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:00,800
the entire project

38
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,240
in 1936.

39
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:03,740
And the result was

40
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:04,630
Hoover Dam,

41
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:07,320
a 726-foot giant

42
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,200
built by moving a river.
